Fanatic: The Fanatic is a zealot of unknown origin. They seem to believe in a supposed group of 'forgotten gods' that shaped the world.
Historian: A noblewoman far from home, the Historian has a keen interest in the depths of the past. Brimming with knowledge, she is willing to share whatever is needed to be known for those who ask.
InfernoGrip: A fully grown Claw from the Inferno, as they mature they seem to develop an ability to manipulate fire. They appear to develop a hardened magma coating as a defensive shell during adulthood. This one has been attracted by a strong scent, hoping to find something.
MireGrip: A fully grown Claw from the Mire, as they mature they seem to develop an ability to manipulate water. They appear to develop a stone coating over time as a defensive shell, yet it quickly gets covered by weeds and other plants. This one has been attracted by a strong scent, hoping to find something.
TruffleToad: A toad in a symbiotic state with underground mushrooms. This blue fungus appears to create a mutually beneficial state between its host and them, resulting in the hosts life being kept. This toad has chosen to willingly accept the growth of these mushrooms into itself for whatever reason.
MushMon: An adventurer's body possessed, mangled, and piloted by the Blight. Their first human host has enlightened these parasitic predators, leaving them hungry for ever more victims.
LeafBeetle: A common insect found roaming grassy plains. Some say that wearing their shell on your clothes brings good luck.
HoneyBee: A bee grown larger than their jungle brethren from a lack of predators. Though less aggressive, their venom is potent and they will attempt to sting you if you get too close.
DragonClaw: The product of an unusual phenomenon within the Inferno. Volcanic rock is seen molding into crude human hands that harass passersby.
HydraClaw: The Mire is a peculiar and extreme place. Even plant matter can take the form of fetid claws to attack outsiders.
BlueMushMound: What appears to be a collective of ordinary blue mushrooms, is actually the lure of a patient predator. Insects and small creatures are drawn to the light and smell of this fungus, unaware of what waits beneath...
Boomshroom: Bizarre, sentient mushrooms with no sense of self-preservation. Moments after spawning, they rush and kamikaze into the first thing they see.
GoAheadTellThemNobodyWillBelieveYou: Being made out of Fluorine, Astatine. Fluorine, Uranium, Carbon, Potassium.
FungoidSwarmer: Newly birthed Fungoids with nimble bodies and soft carapase. They depend on their sense of smell and taste to navigate the world.
FungoidGrunt: Matured Fungoids rarely leave their nests, their larger bodies acting as makeshift barricades. When disturbed, they savagely lunge at anything near them.
FungoidHulk: Crudely sewn together marauders born into the Blight. These menaces once injured split their nerves, becoming two halves from one whole. All as a desperate attempt to survive and spread their malignant curse.
Splinter: Despite their appearance, these are a log of petrified wood animated from the infectious shrooms. It senses through movement in the ground, striking at whatever it senses.
CreeperVine: A cankerous tasteless mass sulking on the ceilings of the Blight. Its connection to the roots of the cavity give it exceptional range. Once it catches wind it fires out its mouth, hooking its toothed orifice into any victim unfortunate enough to cross into the unknown depths.
Witherwing: Cave bats overcome by infection, now slaves to the Blight. They have lost control of their bodies and only serve to spread the host spores.
TumoroidMaw: A twisted basin of bile, formed by the Blight's inner instinct. Rooted into the ground, this gives the Maw a seemingly endless amount of toxins to spew out, forever coating all around it.
TumoroidSentry: A cankerous sniper bursting forth from the walls to strike from beyond sight. The Sentry contorts even the earth itself, splicing roots and mycelium to hold itself against the cavern walls.
TumoroidSpewer: A malignant mutation aimlessly spawned by the Blight to defend its innermost hearts. Cursed with a lack of mobility, the Spewer is forced to crawl about, spewing forth bile to weaken all who approach.
Mushlad: An Isopod taken over by the Mushroom Blight. Despite the Blight’s effects, the Mushlad’s nature is more timid and when threatened, it rolls into a ball and rolls off, rarely to safety.
BlightWorm: One of the greater mysteries involving the Blight's growth. Functioning and behaving like a worm it doesn't look nor behave the part, an uncanny valley of real and unreal. Is it a nerve or a creature? Is it living? Or is it truly dead?
Flamebrute: Particularly unruly resident of the Inferno that stores excess heat in its belly. They are known to spit fireballs at anything that catches their attention.
LivingEmber: Whisper of a past life. Years of isolation and exposure to infernal elements molded this soul into but a dim flame.
ObsidianGolem: Deep in the bowels of their home's blazing ruins, long-dead miners continue their toil, having melted down and become one with their work.
Mosster: Sinister figures that blur the line between animal and plant, adopting both the shape and cruelty of man.
WillowWisp: Whisper of a past life. Left unrecognisable after having its essence warped and drained by an insidious force.
Gator: Ruthless predators residing in the mire, when they catch prey, they violently tear them to shreads with powerful jaws.
Longneck: Close cousin of the Hydras, it sports a disproportionately elongated neck, allowing it to snap at prey no matter where they stand.
TwistedRoot: Living roots born from the Mire's tree. They violently rend and scrape through the thick mud stabbing into trespassers and souls unfortunate to be allured by the tree's siren song.
Terrorvine: Beauty is intoxicatingly deceiving. Where one may see a simple budding lotus, beneath the surface lay a soulless fearless angler ready to choke and strangle life out of whoever falls for its trap.
MireViper: A cunning nocturnal predator of the Mire's many competitive denizens. They chase their prey into bodies of water where it then lunges forth to secure its prize.
GiantMosquito: One of the many mistakes formed from the excess magic in the Mire. These bloated buzzing bugs snatch up anything they see sapping them of everything they hold dear, and if that doesn't work. Their death seals the fate of the captured prey.
RootSucker: Bottom-feeders that suck on the nutritious roots of the Mire's Willow tree. Driven mad and unrecognisably disfigured, something has tainted these poor beasts with hatred.
SoulTotem: When the dreadful tree's roots detect a potential victim, it manifests glowing beacons to lure them in, only to enslave its past victims to drag them towards the same fate.
Apparition: The distorted remains of a soul, regurgitated by the willow roots to feed its own predator.
Depthstalker: Massive, blind amphibians that lurker in the deepest reaches of the Mire. They use vibrations to hunt down their prey.
